src/KOKKOS/pair_brownian_kokkos.cpp:404-408 and :432-436 / :462-466 guard the j-update with `if ((NEIGHFLAG==HALF || NEIGHFLAG==HALFTHREAD) && (NEWTON_PAIR || j < nlocal))`, and :101 `if (neighflag == FULL) request->enable_full();` allows FULL (EnabledNeighFlags = FULL|HALFTHREAD|HALF, pair_brownian_kokkos.h:41).  Each visit of a pair draws fresh numbers at :354/:379/:385/:444/:450 via `rand_gen.drand()`.
The CPU style uses a half list and applies -f to i and +f to j from the SAME draw (src/COLLOID/pair_brownian.cpp:254-267), and warns when that symmetry is lost (:445-446 'Pair brownian needs newton pair on for momentum conservation').
The analogous stochastic KOKKOS pair styles refuse the configuration outright, e.g. src/KOKKOS/pair_dpd_ext_kokkos.cpp:94-95:
